monolith (2.11.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New upstream release
  * TLS is now rustls on a statically linked AWS-LC (upstream moved to
    reqwest 0.13), so the binary no longer links the system OpenSSL.
  * Add ca-certificates dependency; 2.11.0 panics at startup without a
    system CA store, even on a local file.
  * Build with cc 1.5.1: cc 1.6.0 lets dpkg's -O2 reach aws-lc-sys's
    jitterentropy, which refuses to compile optimised.

 -- pkg.haus archive <archive@pkg.haus>  Mon, 05 Oct 2026 07:49:27 +0200

monolith (2.10.1-2) unstable; urgency=high

  * Link against the system OpenSSL. The previous build statically linked a
    private OpenSSL 3.4.1 into a package for a suite shipping 3.5.x, declared no
    libssl dependency, and could not be reached by a Debian security update.
  * Build reproducibly: identical bytes across build path, hostname, locale,
    timezone, umask, CPU count and file ordering.
  * Record the Rust toolchain among the build dependencies, so the build can be
    reproduced from its .buildinfo.

 -- pkg.haus archive <archive@pkg.haus>  Wed, 02 Sep 2026 11:04:53 +0200

